Burrow: Haiku tunnel units, tunnel routes, point-to-point peers and IPv6.

- Create the tun/<n> interface on demand and remove it on exit, so no
  manual "ifconfig tun/0 up" is needed and several tunnels can coexist.
- Put VPN routes on the tunnel interface. The HaikuPorts patch put every
  route on the default gateway's interface, so pushed routes left through
  the Ethernet card. Only routes via the original gateway stay there.
- IPv6 routes use the tunnel (or the server-route interface) instead of a
  NULL r6->iface, and IPv6 addresses are configured with ifconfig inet6.
- net30/p2p topologies configure the remote end as the interface peer.

